# What must NOT enter the build context.
#
# node_modules is the one that bites first: copied in, pnpm refuses to remove it without a
# TTY and the build dies — and if it had succeeded, a Linux image would be running macOS
# binaries. Build outputs are next: copying a host `dist` means the image can ship code the
# Dockerfile never compiled.
#
# A .dockerignore is a DENY list, so the failure mode is the safe one: forget an entry and
# the build is slower, not wrong. The opposite mistake — excluding something the build needs
# — is the one that produces an image missing a file, which is how a sibling repo ran three
# days stale before anyone noticed. Everything here is excluded because it is harmful or
# useless, never merely large.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build outputs. The image compiles its own.
dist
**/dist
dev-dist
**/dev-dist
conformance-dist
**/conformance-dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/.turbo

# Never, under any circumstances.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# No value inside an image.
.git
.github
.githooks
.changeset
.claude
docs
test
**/*.test.ts
coverage
.vitest
